			<div class="content" id="post-content-2501610">
									

<p>here's what's going on.</p>
<p>Mr Escoffier was a Tintin fanatic who tried to summon lovecraftian monstrosities, but their minds accidentally got trapped within the <em>Tintin</em> book.</p>
<p>When you open the book to the page in question, the monstrosities' (<em>Tintin</em>-based) bodies instantiate, but remain mindless and inert, because their minds are trapped in the panels of the book. They keep screaming and ranting in <em>Tintin</em>-based vocabularies, and they can't even stop making <em>Tintin</em> allusions.</p>
<p>Their bodies are based on the four main characters of <em>Tintin</em> (three humans and a dog): Tintin (orange hair and light blue outfit), Captain Haddock (black hair and dark blue outfit), Professor Calculus (black hair and green outfit), and Snowy (white dog). The whiskey is because Captain Haddock was a heavy drinker, and they're giant barnacles because one of Captain Haddock's character traits was his ridiculously ornate swearing, including a phrase which was translated into English as &quot;BILLIONS OF BLUE BLISTERING BARNACLES&quot;.</p>
<p>If the monstrosity minds could control the bodies, they could wreak great terror on this pathetic world. But they can't. They can't control the bodies, they can't access them, they can't even make the bodies die or de-instantiate. All they can do is alter the text in the speech bubbles on two pages of one copy of one graphic novel.</p>
<p>And then you close the book, and the entities' minds are forced back into dormancy.</p>

